    "https://franklinpierceuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/yMQcq7jgfL/Graduate-Assistant-At-FPU-Only-Admissions-20262027": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant at FPU Only - Admissions 2026-2027",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant at FPU Only - Admissions 2026-2027 - Franklin Pierce University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Welcome to the Franklin Pierce University Job Board. We post all Faculty, Staff, Student Employment, and Graduate Assistant positions on this site. If you are looking for a collaborative environment where you have the ability to influence the student and workplace experience every day and where the contributions of a diverse group of individuals are highly valued, come see what we have to offer. We offer a competitive benefits package. Click here to review our Benefits Guide. As an Equal Opportunity employer, Franklin Pierce recognizes the impact of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, backgrounds and perspectives. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, pregnancy, age, disability gender identity and expression, protected veteran status or any other status protected by law. If you are unable to submit an application because of incompatible assistive technology or a disability, please contact us at [email protected] or 603-899-4075. We will make every effort to respond to your request for disability assistance as soon as possible. Graduate Assistant at FPU Only - Admissions 2026-2027 Rindge, NH Part Time Admissions Student (College) Share Requires an undergraduate degree from an accredited institution and acceptance into a graduate studies program at Franklin Pierce University (acceptance must be confirmed before the candidate is considered). Job Summary: Participate in training as a Student Ambassador. Provide Campus Tours, as needed to individuals and groups. Meet with prospective students and their family members during campus visits to provide timely and accurate information about Franklin Pierce University, our programs and services. This includes weekend visitation. Assist with the training of new student employees. Coordinate the recruitment, selection and training of overnight student hosts. Assist in planning and execution of recruitment events including, but not limited to the Overnight Program, Accepted Student events, Tour & Tailgates, among other visitation programs. Create engaging content for events that highlights campus life for prospective students. Design, implement and analyze surveys to measure effectiveness of on campus programs. Distribute survey results to administrators, as necessary. Other duties as assigned Experience and Qualifications: Must have a Bachelors degree and be a matriculated graduate student at Franklin Pierce University. Strong communication skills, especially verbal communication ability desired. He/she must be able to work independently, be productive and competent in a busy work environment that demands strong organizational and multi-tasking skills, and ability to handle confidential information. Good technical skills. Experience with databases and MS Office. Good Excel skills required. Required Workdays: Monday - Friday, but will include some Saturday and/or Sunday Hours/Pay Full Time (20 hours) Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Cover Letter * Does your Financial Aid package include Federal Work Study? * -- No answer -- Yes No I don't know Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
