be required to work some weekends, holidays and mandatory days. Experience and Qualifications: Must maintain a high level of integrity and the ability to maintain confidentiality and discretion.  Maintain acceptable work habits, punctuality and regularity of attendance to arrive and leave work on time and observe established break times and lunch periods. Ability to effectively communicate and follow oral instructions in English.  Ability to effectively read written instructions, signs and products in English. Adhere to University protocol relating to safety procedures. Adhere to the policies and procedures established by Franklin Pierce University. Special Notes: Accept and render constructive criticism in a professional manner.  Carry out all responsibilities and objectives in a professional manner.  Other duties as assigned. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
