    "https://franklinpierceuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/R3CMRb6tlp/Students-Only-At-FPU-WarehousePostal-Student-Assistant": {
      "title": "Students Only at FPU:  Warehouse/Postal Student Assistant",
      "description": "Students Only at FPU:  Warehouse/Postal Student Assistant - Franklin Pierce University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Welcome to the Franklin Pierce University Job Board. We post all Faculty, Staff, Student Employment, and Graduate Assistant positions on this site. If you are looking for a collaborative environment where you have the ability to influence the student and workplace experience every day and where the contributions of a diverse group of individuals are highly valued, come see what we have to offer. We offer a competitive benefits package. Click here to review our Benefits Guide. As an Equal Opportunity employer, Franklin Pierce recognizes the impact of a diverse community and encourages applications from individuals with varied experiences, backgrounds and perspectives. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, pregnancy, age, disability gender identity and expression, protected veteran status or any other status protected by law. If you are unable to submit an application because of incompatible assistive technology or a disability, please contact us at [email protected] or 603-899-4075. We will make every effort to respond to your request for disability assistance as soon as possible. Students Only at FPU:  Warehouse/Postal Student Assistant Rindge, NH Part Time Processing Center Student (College) Share Position Summary: Warehouse/Postal Student Assistants will deliver mail/packages to campus post office and all departments/offices on campus. Student Assistants will drive the cargo mail van to make deliveries on campus as well as to deliver and pick up from the Rindge Post Office. Student Assistants may also deliver paper, bottled water, print materials from the Copy Center, and shredding bins as needed throughout campus. Student Assistants may also assist in the Copy Center with various projects. Student Assistants help to maintain organization of the Warehouse as well. 4-10 hours per week Qualifications: Student Assistants must have 3-years of driving experience and a clean driving record. Student Assistants must be able to lift up to 50 pounds. Student Assistants with strong organizational skills, excellent communication skills, and those with a desire to work as part of a team will be the most successful candidates. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address * Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file References: Please enter names and contact information: * Upload your cover letter here or in the above field. Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
